# Pulumi ComponentResource: Application Stack (TypeScript)

Below is a production-ready implementation of a ComponentResource wrapping S3, RDS PostgreSQL, and IAM resources, with dev/prod differentiation via stack config.

## Project Structure

```
.
├── Pulumi.yaml
├── Pulumi.dev.yaml
├── Pulumi.prod.yaml
├── src/
│   ├── index.ts           # Main stack entry point
│   └── appStack.ts        # ComponentResource definition
└── package.json
```

## 1. ComponentResource Definition (`src/appStack.ts`)

```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";

interface AppStackArgs {
  environment: "dev" | "prod";
  dbInstanceClass: string;
  dbAllocatedStorage: number;
  dbMultiAZ: boolean;
  s3ReplicationRegion?: string;
}

export class AppStack extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
  public bucket: aws.s3.Bucket;
  public dbInstance: aws.rds.Instance;
  public serviceRole: aws.iam.Role;
  public serviceRolePolicy: aws.iam.RolePolicy;

  constructor(
    name: string,
    args: AppStackArgs,
    opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions
  ) {
    super("custom:app:Stack", name, {}, opts);

    const config = pulumi.getStack();
    const projectName = pulumi.getProject();
    const resourceTags = {
      Environment: args.environment,
      Project: projectName,
      ManagedBy: "Pulumi",
    };

    // ========== S3 Bucket ==========
    this.bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket(
      `${name}-bucket`,
      {
        bucket: `${projectName}-${args.environment}-${aws.getCallerIdentity().then(id => id.accountId)}-assets`,
        tags: resourceTags,
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    // Enable versioning
    new aws.s3.BucketVersioningV2(
      `${name}-versioning`,
      {
        bucket: this.bucket.id,
        versioningConfiguration: {
          status: "Enabled",
        },
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    // Enable server-side encryption (AES-256)
    new aws.s3.BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2(
      `${name}-encryption`,
      {
        bucket: this.bucket.id,
        rules: [
          {
            applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: {
              sseAlgorithm: "AES256",
            },
          },
        ],
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    // Block all public access
    new aws.s3.BucketPublicAccessBlock(
      `${name}-pab`,
      {
        bucket: this.bucket.id,
        blockPublicAcls: true,
        blockPublicPolicy: true,
        ignorePublicAcls: true,
        restrictPublicBuckets: true,
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    // Cross-region replication for prod
    if (args.environment === "prod" && args.s3ReplicationRegion) {
      const replicationRole = new aws.iam.Role(
        `${name}-replication-role`,
        {
          assumeRolePolicy: aws.iam
            .getPolicyDocument({
              statements: [
                {
                  effect: "Allow",
                  principals: [
                    {
                      type: "Service",
                      identifiers: ["s3.amazonaws.com"],
                    },
                  ],
                  actions: ["sts:AssumeRole"],
                },
              ],
            })
            .then((doc) => doc.json),
          tags: resourceTags,
        },
        { parent: this }
      );

      new aws.iam.RolePolicy(
        `${name}-replication-policy`,
        {
          role: replicationRole.id,
          policy: aws.iam
            .getPolicyDocument({
              statements: [
                {
                  effect: "Allow",
                  actions: [
                    "s3:GetReplicationConfiguration",
                    "s3:ListBucket",
                  ],
                  resources: [this.bucket.arn],
                },
                {
                  effect: "Allow",
                  actions: [
                    "s3:GetObjectVersionForReplication",
                    "s3:GetObjectVersionAcl",
                    "s3:GetObjectVersionTagging",
                  ],
                  resources: [pulumi.interpolate`${this.bucket.arn}/*`],
                },
                {
                  effect: "Allow",
                  actions: [
                    "s3:ReplicateObject",
                    "s3:ReplicateDelete",
                    "s3:ReplicateTags",
                  ],
                  resources: [
                    pulumi.interpolate`arn:aws:s3:::${projectName}-${args.environment}-replica/*`,
                  ],
                },
              ],
            })
            .then((doc) => doc.json),
        },
        { parent: this }
      );

      new aws.s3.BucketReplicationConfig(
        `${name}-replication`,
        {
          role: replicationRole.arn,
          bucket: this.bucket.id,
          rules: [
            {
              id: "replicate-all",
              filter: {},
              status: "Enabled",
              priority: 1,
              destination: {
                bucket: pulumi.interpolate`arn:aws:s3:::${projectName}-${args.environment}-replica`,
                replicationTime: {
                  status: "Enabled",
                  time: 15,
                },
                metrics: {
                  status: "Enabled",
                  eventThreshold: 15,
                },
              },
            },
          ],
        },
        { parent: this }
      );
    }

    // ========== RDS PostgreSQL Instance ==========
    const dbPassword = new pulumi.Config().requireSecret(
      "dbPassword"
    );

    this.dbInstance = new aws.rds.Instance(
      `${name}-db`,
      {
        allocatedStorage: args.dbAllocatedStorage,
        storageType: "gp3",
        engine: "postgres",
        engineVersion: "15.4",
        instanceClass: args.dbInstanceClass,
        dbName: "appdb",
        username: "postgres",
        password: dbPassword,
        skipFinalSnapshot: args.environment === "dev",
        finalSnapshotIdentifier:
          args.environment === "prod"
            ? pulumi.interpolate`${projectName}-${args.environment}-final-${Date.now()}`
            : undefined,
        multiAz: args.dbMultiAZ,
        storageEncrypted: true,
        backupRetentionPeriod: args.environment === "prod" ? 30 : 7,
        deletionProtection: args.environment === "prod",
        publiclyAccessible: false,
        enableCloudwatchLogsExports: ["postgresql"],
        performanceInsightsEnabled: args.environment === "prod",
        tags: resourceTags,
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    // ========== IAM Role for Service Accounts ==========
    this.serviceRole = new aws.iam.Role(
      `${name}-service-role`,
      {
        assumeRolePolicy: aws.iam
          .getPolicyDocument({
            statements: [
              {
                effect: "Allow",
                principals: [
                  {
                    type: "Service",
                    identifiers: ["ec2.amazonaws.com"],
                  },
                ],
                actions: ["sts:AssumeRole"],
              },
            ],
          })
          .then((doc) => doc.json),
        tags: resourceTags,
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    // Least-privilege service policy
    const servicePolicyStatements =
      args.environment === "prod"
        ? // Prod: minimal, resource-specific
          [
            {
              effect: "Allow" as const,
              actions: ["s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
              resources: [
                this.bucket.arn,
                pulumi.interpolate`${this.bucket.arn}/*`,
              ],
            },
            {
              effect: "Allow" as const,
              actions: ["rds-db:connect"],
              resources: [this.dbInstance.arn],
            },
          ]
        : // Dev: broader but still no wildcard actions
          [
            {
              effect: "Allow" as const,
              actions: [
                "s3:GetObject",
                "s3:PutObject",
                "s3:DeleteObject",
                "s3:ListBucket",
              ],
              resources: [
                this.bucket.arn,
                pulumi.interpolate`${this.bucket.arn}/*`,
              ],
            },
            {
              effect: "Allow" as const,
              actions: ["rds-db:connect", "rds:DescribeDBInstances"],
              resources: [this.dbInstance.arn],
            },
          ];

    this.serviceRolePolicy = new aws.iam.RolePolicy(
      `${name}-service-policy`,
      {
        role: this.serviceRole.id,
        policy: aws.iam
          .getPolicyDocument({
            statements: servicePolicyStatements,
          })
          .then((doc) => doc.json),
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    this.registerOutputs({
      bucketName: this.bucket.bucket,
      bucketArn: this.bucket.arn,
      dbEndpoint: this.dbInstance.endpoint,
      dbArn: this.dbInstance.arn,
      serviceRoleArn: this.serviceRole.arn,
      serviceRoleName: this.serviceRole.name,
    });
  }
}
```

## 2. Stack Configuration Files

### `Pulumi.dev.yaml`

```yaml
config:
  aws:region: us-east-1
  app:dbInstanceClass: db.t3.micro
  app:dbAllocatedStorage: "20"
  app:dbMultiAZ: "false"
  dbPassword:
    secure: AQEAA...  # Run: pulumi config set --secret dbPassword '<password>'
```

### `Pulumi.prod.yaml`

```yaml
config:
  aws:region: us-east-1
  app:dbInstanceClass: db.t3.medium
  app:dbAllocatedStorage: "100"
  app:dbMultiAZ: "true"
  app:s3ReplicationRegion: us-west-2
  dbPassword:
    secure: AQEAA...  # Different secret per stack
```

### `Pulumi.yaml`

```yaml
name: myapp
runtime: nodejs
description: Application infrastructure with ComponentResource
```

## 3. Main Stack Entry Point (`src/index.ts`)

```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { AppStack } from "./appStack";

const cfg = new pulumi.Config("app");
const awsConfig = new pulumi.Config("aws");

const appStack = new AppStack("app", {
  environment: (pulumi.getStack() as "dev" | "prod") || "dev",
  dbInstanceClass: cfg.require("dbInstanceClass"),
  dbAllocatedStorage: cfg.requireNumber("dbAllocatedStorage"),
  dbMultiAZ: cfg.requireBoolean("dbMultiAZ"),
  s3ReplicationRegion: cfg.get("s3ReplicationRegion") || undefined,
});

export const bucketName = appStack.bucket.bucket;
export const bucketArn = appStack.bucket.arn;
export const dbEndpoint = appStack.dbInstance.endpoint;
export const dbArn = appStack.dbInstance.arn;
export const serviceRoleArn = appStack.serviceRole.arn;
```

## 4. Package Dependencies (`package.json`)

```json
{
  "name": "myapp-iac",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "dependencies": {
    "@pulumi/aws": "^6.x",
    "@pulumi/pulumi": "^3.x"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "typescript": "^5.x"
  }
}
```

## Deployment

```bash
# Install dependencies
npm install

# Set secrets (one-time per stack)
pulumi config set --secret dbPassword 'SecurePassword123!'

# Deploy dev
pulumi stack select dev
pulumi up

# Deploy prod (independent)
pulumi stack select prod
pulumi config set --secret dbPassword 'ProdSecurePassword456!'
pulumi up
```

## Acceptance Criteria Met

| Criterion | Implementation |
|-----------|---|
| **S3 versioning** | `BucketVersioningV2` with status `Enabled` |
| **S3 encryption** | `BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2` (AES-256) |
| **S3 no public access** | `BucketPublicAccessBlock` blocks all ACLs and policies |
| **RDS deletion protection** | `deletionProtection: true` on prod only |
| **RDS backup retention** | 7 days dev, 30 days prod |
| **RDS not publicly accessible** | `publiclyAccessible: false` |
| **RDS encryption** | `storageEncrypted: true` |
| **RDS multi-AZ (prod)** | `multiAz: true` on prod, `false` on dev |
| **IAM least privilege** | Resource-specific ARNs; prod has no wildcard actions |
| **Secrets** | Database password via `pulumi config set --secret` |
| **Environment isolation** | Separate stacks (`dev.yaml`, `prod.yaml`); independent state |
| **S3 replication (prod)** | Conditional replication role + config for prod only |

The ComponentResource encapsulates infrastructure as a reusable unit, stack configs drive env-specific behavior, and resource tagging enables cost tracking per environment.
